WEBVTT

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.090
On the left!

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.240
Don't get flanked!

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:08.980
Got it.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.320
What <i>is</i> this "Black Blizzard"?

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.650
To think even the Maze Pass would be
this infected by the Black Element...

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.480
They can regenerate?!

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.400
It's because of this Black Blizzard.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.360
Striking them down isn't enough.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.200
Marina, are you ready?

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.400
Healing power within me,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:05.670
power of life, imbue my staff 
and grant life to those before me.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.420
Wow.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.420
That was healing magic, wasn't it?

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.080
You can destroy those
skeleton bastards with it?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.230
They <i>are</i> undead, after all.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.180
So even you can be useful
in combat sometimes, huh?

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.240
"Sometimes"?

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.050
Is that how you see me?

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.780
All you ever do is trip over.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.780
What's that?

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.250
Take this!

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.270
All you gotta do is burn them bones!

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.160
Aram!

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:11.560
<b>Snowy Mountain Screams</b>

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.430
They don't seem to have been buried alive.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.030
I can't believe the snow couldn't handle
one of my weakest spells.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:16.390
Talk about pathetic.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:20.270
No, you overdid it, Velnar.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.670
Shut up.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.960
Better too much than too little.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.570
That's enough, you two.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.140
What should we do?

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.700
Should we go look for the two of them?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.050
Why don't we meet up
with the earth sprites first?

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:40.590
We'd be better off with the help of 
those familiar with these mountains.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.040
You're right.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.430
I'm sure the Captain would do the same.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.630
I agree, too.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.470
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.680
<i>The Black Element is strong
in these mountains.</i>

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.800
<i>Yuri...</i>

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.650
Damn.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:09.790
Are you cold?

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.220
Just stay in there.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.550
Hey, Yuri, do you know what this is?

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.430
No. I've never seen anything like it before.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.290
It's not dangerous, is it?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.580
I don't know.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:27.630
But I don't sense any evil from it, 
so I think it's safe to keep around.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:31.470
We're in this mess because
we tried to protect you, you know.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.730
You'd better be grateful, Furball.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.730
Furball?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.520
That's what I've named it,
since it <i>is</i> a ball of fur.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.450
Named it? Are you going to keep it?

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.310
No, I wasn't planning to.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.830
Maybe you're not, but it looks like
that thing has already made up its mind.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.000
Hey.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.200
Stop it.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.790
It's your responsibility now.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.120
What's up?

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.500
The blizzard's getting worse.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.470
Let's stop here and set up camp.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.560
Wait, Yuri.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.990
Let's keep going. We're probably close to...

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:20.390
No, the cold saps your energy
more than you'd think.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.430
Let's dig a snow cave here
and wait for the weather to improve.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:25.470
Got it?

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.840
O-Okay.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.700
Yuri's missing?!

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:38.290
Along with a boy named Aram, 
who recently joined us.

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.390
All right.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:42.540
We'll send out a search team right away.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.830
Do any of you want to come along?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:45.810
Yeah.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:51.190
Kiki, can you let the fire sprites know, too?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:55.850
It's a hassle, but fine.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.720
Since it's for Yuri's sake.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.610
Thank you.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.260
Got it.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:10.620
Sorry to make you come this far
into the Pass during an emergency.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.740
We just happened to find something huge.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.950
Be careful with it.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.450
This is an incredible treasure.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.450
Hey!

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.450
Can anyone hear me?

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:30.820
Hey!

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.810
Damn it.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.970
I can't get through.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.920
The Black Blizzard might be
hindering communications.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:43.770
Hey, Yuri, I really think
we should keep walking.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:49.570
No, the golden rule for when you're lost
is to stay right where you are.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.740
But...

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.740
I'm sure Phoena and the rest have
enlisted the help of the earth sprites

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.620
and are looking for us right now.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.290
The earth sprites?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.420
Are you sure they'll help?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.630
Besides, in this weather, 
our friends might not...

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.870
Don't worry.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:09.230
They've fought by my side all this time.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.010
So I trust them.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:12.710
Bah.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.010
Nothing.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.210
That wasn't nothing.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.090
Shut up.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.500
I was just feeling a bit envious...

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:26.570
of your confidence in your friends.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:35.100
I don't trust them that much yet.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.910
Aram.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.900
I've never had friends.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:44.920
I've always had to do everything for myself.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:52.710
At some point, everyone comes across
a situation they can't deal with alone.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.670
Whether they have someone to help
when that happens,

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:59.580
and whether they can trust them fully,

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:02.600
probably determines a person's true strength.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:07.050
Is that what you call a bond?

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.500
I'm not sure.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:09.760
It's not?

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:10.740
Who knows?

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:15.730
That's probably something you have 
to find out for yourself, Aram.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.690
Bah. You spoilsport.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.510
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.820
<i>You'll find it yourself someday,</i>

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:25.710
<i>a light that's right for you.</i>

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.560
Maybe we should have gone with them.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:39.220
I'd like to, but first we need to do
what we came here to do.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:45.230
To ask the earth and fire sprites to
help the Black King Suppression Army.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:46.560
Yes.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.510
And one other thing.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:53.730
Why did Fatima instruct us to come here?

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.180
Could it be...

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:58.720
Marina, don't you sense something?

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.960
I do.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.740
It's an artifact with immense magical power.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.990
We need to figure out what this is.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:09.100
That must be why we were sent here.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:19.160
"Deep, deep within the 
depths of the Maze Pass,

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.640
there lies a sword of hope.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.100
A blade, cutting through the darkness."

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.720
Cutting through the darkness?

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.610
There's no doubt.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:31.140
This will surely be of use to us.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:35.230
Don't fall asleep, Aram.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.640
I wasn't sleeping.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:43.210
If you're sleepy, why don't we
play word chain or something?

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.840
Word chain?

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.160
Me and you?

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.370
Is that weird?

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.710
No, it's not weird, but...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.450
I mean...

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:58.370
I can't think of anything else 
to do in this situation.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:01.930
Okay.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.410
Fine. Let's play word chain.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:06.350
But first...

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.050
Aram?

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.890
It's so cold.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.510
I gotta go take a leak.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.020
Did you hear that? "Word chain."

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:23.000
Yuri's a lot more normal 
in person than I thought.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.900
Don't you think so, Furball?

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:29.410
Furball?

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:30.850
Hey!

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.200
Furball!

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:34.180
Where'd you go?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.250
Damn it, that idiot.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.110
Yuri!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.570
<i>You're kidding me.</i>

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:45.820
Yuri!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.830
Furball!

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.150
Hey!

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:58.980
Shuza, sir, I come with a message 
from Holy Princess Juliana.

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:02.770
A Black King Suppression Army?

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:03.730
Yes.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:12.370
She requests your help in ridding
the continent of the Black Army for good.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.140
I see.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.290
Very well.

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:21.310
I shall give you my reply now.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.720
Aram!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.540
Aram!

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.990
Did he get himself lost?

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:36.310
I have to go find him.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.970
<i>Wait, do I really have to go?</i>

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:46.040
<i>I told him not to move when lost.</i>

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:49.210
<i>If he got lost after that,
it's his own responsibility.</i>

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:52.150
<i>Even if he froze to death, 
it wouldn't be my fault.</i>

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:56.030
What was I thinking just now?

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.490
Damn it.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.610
I'm not giving up.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.280
Just relax, already.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:22.600
Why do you resist?

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.340
You've already lost.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:27.490
I haven't lost yet.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.180
Liar.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.100
"Trust your friends"?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:32.670
"Trust your allies"?

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:34.060
You can't be serious.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:38.420
You couldn't even trust 
your friends or allies yourself.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:43.050
That's right. You doubted this world.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.320
You doubted the people living in it.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.640
You doubted whether it's worth

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:54.680
going through the pain and 
suffering to save it.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.310
No!

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:59.740
You're a husk of a hero.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:02.930
In fact, you're a puppet,
held hostage by the word "hero"

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:06.440
and played like a fiddle by fate.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:11.190
And you, yourself, are more 
sick of yourself than anyone.

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:15.860
This world tasked you with saving it 
 because you are a hero.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:19.940
"Save the world," they all asked.

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:22.860
If they ask for help, a hero must do so.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.600
For that is the reason for
a hero's very existence.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:28.840
But, at the same time, 
you came to the realization:

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:33.670
that there is no one to save a hero.

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.140
Shut up!

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:44.720
That is why you lost to the Black King.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:46.990
And that is why, now,

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.820
you are turning black yourself.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:58.710
It's useless to resist.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.530
I know everything.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:04.290
After all, I am you.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.470
Give it up.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:11.930
You, who despaired at being a hero,
are destined for the black world.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.080
You belong there.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.140
No, you don't!

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:22.520
Are you all right, Yuri?

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:37.600
<i>I see.</i>

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.830
<i>They were the ones filling 
my mind with fear.</i>

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.970
Don't touch them, Aram.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:47.170
I have to defeat them myself.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.630
Why?

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:55.430
Come on, Yuri, you said one's strength 
lies in letting others help them.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:59.140
I don't really know what it 
means to have bonds yet.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:04.850
But I do know one thing:
I want to be of help to you.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:08.070
So, right now, my sword is your sword.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.330
Me defeating them is the same 
as you defeating them.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.400
Am I wrong?

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.240
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:22.260
<i>Aram, you never needed to look for it.</i>

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.690
Seize the light!

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:51.810
Aram.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:56.160
Hey, Yuri, was that a chain attack?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.900
I did it!

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:01.910
Awesome!

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.160
Awesome!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.540
I combined moves with you!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.250
Good job, Aram.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.400
Oh, right, is your arm okay?

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:12.870
It's not a problem.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:14.040
More importantly…

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.390
Aren't you Baltazari?

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:26.630
Who is it that calls me Baltazari?

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:29.470
Begone, blasted snow!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:36.460
Oh, Yuri, is that you?

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.260
It's been a while.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.410
You know this weird old man, Yuri?

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:43.310
Baltazari.

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:46.070
He's the master of Fatima, 
whom we met at the Sage Tower,

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:48.250
and the previous Fate Sage.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:50.460
That naked chick's master?

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:53.010
Actually, that makes sense.

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:05.440
Furball!

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.070
Where did you get to, stupid?

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.980
Did the Black Blizzard blow you off course?

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:17.160
You seem to be drowning 
in dark waters right now.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.990
The more you fight it, 
the deeper you'll fall.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.360
It may be easier to
let yourself be taken away.

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:25.950
No, so long as there's hope,
I'll continue to fight.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:31.460
But hope, at times, may take
a person's life with its powerful light.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.440
Despite this, you would still continue?

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:37.470
If I'm to be killed by hope, 
I shall die happy.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:42.480
Well said!

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:47.560
If that is how determined you are,
then I have nothing to say.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.220
Go forth, hero.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:55.170
I'll give you some good advice 
in return for the entertainment.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:59.470
You've defeated a guardian dragon 
in the past, have you not?

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.490
Yes, at the desert oasis.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:05.660
A new dragon will appear there someday.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.310
Make your way there.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.530
Captain!

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:12.160
Captain!

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:13.870
Aram!

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:15.550
Hey!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.540
Guys, we found the Captain and Aram!

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.950
Baltazari...

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:26.760
You were right.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:30.140
You said your friends would find you.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.220
Yeah.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:33.860
But don't forget, Aram.

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.480
They're not <i>my</i> friends.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.700
They're <i>our</i> friends.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:58.670
We earth sprites will join up with the
Suppression Army as soon as we're ready.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:00.550
Thanks, Olga.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.360
We fire sprites will, too.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.400
Thank you, Rolo.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.350
And you can leave the artifact up to us.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.840
We'll take good care of it.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.690
Thank you very much.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.270
Sure thing.

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.060
What, really?

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.390
You forged that sword?

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:21.070
You're a bit rough, but you have talent.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.400
Train well.

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:30.510
Come on, Captain, drink up.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:33.280
You had us all worried.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.590
I'm glad you're both safe.

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:39.630
Yeah, who knows what would have 
happened if I'd been all by myself?

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.500
But Yuri was there for me.

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.340
And Furball, too.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.520
Furball?

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:47.680
You have terrible taste in names.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.340
Hey, Marina's on the ground again.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:55.280
Hey!

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:56.800
Did that thing just...

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:59.640
You're so weird.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:02.560
I'm telling you, that furball...

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:03.760
Want more?

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:04.940
Thanks.

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:09.110
I feel like getting separated and lost

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:12.290
actually made me grow closer to everyone.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.920
So, y'know, uh...

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.090
Thanks and stuff, Yuri.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.680
No, thank you.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:24.150
I'm glad I got to know you, Aram.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.180
So we're finally going to Soul Island.

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:43.480
Yeah, we're going get Pirika back.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:45.810
I've never been across the sea.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.030
What's that?

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:52.900
Shuza.

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:56.410
I'm glad you're here.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.660
Are you going to join
the Black King Suppression Army?

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:03.150
Hand over the Chain Chronicle.

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:13.510
I'm going to defeat the Black King 
and rule Yggdra myself.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>The Nadir of Anguish</b>

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.900
Fate is set in motion.
